    {
      "text": "they straightway left their nets, and followed him, Matt. 4:20. Take no thought for your life, what ye shall eat, Matt. 6:25. he that loseth his life for my sake shall find it, Matt. 10:39 (16:25; D&C 98:13). sell that thou hast, and give to the poor, Matt. 19:21. every one that hath forsaken houses, or brethren, Matt. 19:29. whosoever will be chief among you, let him be your servant, Matt. 20:27 (D&C 50:26). I will follow thee whithersoever thou goest, Luke 9:57. whosoever … forsaketh not all … cannot be my disciple, Luke 14:33. I am among you as he that serveth, Luke 22:27. I lay down my life, that I might take it again, John 10:17. worthy to suffer shame for his name, Acts 5:41. great things he must suffer for my name’s sake, Acts 9:16. sufferings of this present time … compared with the glory which shall be revealed, Rom. 8:18. present your bodies a living sacrifice, Rom. 12:1. being persecuted, we suffer it, 1 Cor. 4:12. first gave their own selves to the Lord, 2 Cor. 8:5. five times received I forty stripes save one, 2 Cor. 11:24. by love serve one another, Gal. 5:13. hath given himself for us an offering and a sacrifice, Eph. 5:2. for whom I have suffered the loss of all things, Philip. 3:8. gave himself a ransom for all, 1 Tim. 2:6 (Titus 2:14). put away sin by the sacrifice of himself, Heb. 9:26 (2 Ne. 2:7). offered one sacrifice for sins for ever, Heb. 10:12. with such sacrifices God is well pleased, Heb. 13:16. offer up spiritual sacrifices, 1 Pet. 2:5. Christ also suffered for us, leaving us an example, 1 Pet. 2:21. his own self bare our sins in his own body, 1 Pet. 2:24. better … that ye suffer for well doing, than for evil, 1 Pet. 3:17.",
